        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_987430295.1",
        "comments": "The assembly of Nessorhamphus ingolfianus (fNesIng1) is based on 47X PacBio data and 134X Arima Hi-C data generated as part of the ATLASea programme (https://www.atlasea.fr). The assembly process included the following steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, removal of contaminant sequences using Context, removal of haplotypic duplications using purge_dups, and Hi-C-based scaffolding with YaHS. In total, 1 contigs was identified as contaminants (bacterial, archaeal, or viral), totaling 0.028 Mb (with the largest being 0.028 Mb). Additionally, 304 regions totaling 88.245 Mb (with the largest being 2.495 Mb) were identified as haplotypic duplications and removed. Mitochondrial genome was assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analyzed and manually improved using Pretext. During manual curation, 2 haplotypic regions were removed, totaling 1.233Mb (with the largest being 0.748Mb). Note that chromosomes 2 and 6 contain substantially more assembly gaps than the other chromosomes and exhibit an unusual coverage pattern, suggesting that they may represent sex chromosomes. In addition, the organization of chromosome 2 remains uncertain, as the available Hi-C data do not provide sufficient support to confidently validate its structure. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by Hi-C data were named in order of size.",
